<title>USA: Pittsburgh sees $24 mln surplus, first since 1990.</title>
<headline>Pittsburgh sees $24 mln surplus, first since 1990.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The city of Pittsburgh is out of the red.</p>
<p>For the first time since 1990, the city has a positive balance in its general fund, according to city Controller Tom Flaherty.</p>
<p>Flaherty said the city has a surplus of almost $24 million. He attributed the improvement to cost cutting and revenue raising effort by Mayor Tom Murphy.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
